---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const entries = await getCollection('research');
const studies = entries.filter((e) => e.id.endsWith('study-objective'));
const inputs = entries.filter((e) => !e.id.endsWith('study-objective'));
---

<Base
  title="What is this?"
  eyebrow="All about this system"
  intro="An internal reference for the SCB Easy overhaul. It renders the project's research artefacts straight from source, so it is never out of step with them."
>
  <p>
    Content is read from <code>product-context/</code> when the site builds. Nothing here is
    typed twice, which is what stops the site drifting from the artefacts it describes. To
    change a page, edit the markdown.
  </p>

  <h2>What's here today</h2>

  <dl class="counts">
    <div><dt>Studies</dt><dd>{studies.length}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Inputs</dt><dd>{inputs.length}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Artefacts</dt><dd>{entries.length}</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <ul class="list">
    {
      entries.map((entry) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`/${entry.id}`}>{entry.data.name ?? entry.data.title ?? entry.id}</a>
          {entry.data.status && <span class="tag">{entry.data.status}</span>}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>What isn't here yet</h2>
  <p>
    Design system documentation — elements, components, patterns, guidelines. Those sections
    are listed in the navigation but empty on purpose. Writing component documentation before
    there are components to document means writing it twice.
  </p>

  <h2>Reading the artefacts</h2>
  <p>
    Each research page carries a metadata strip: evidence quality, confidence, and whether it
    is a source of truth. Read it before citing anything. Desk research cannot ground a user
    need, and the artefacts say so where it applies.
  </p>

  <style>
    .counts {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--p-spacing-07);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--s-border-subtle);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--s-border-subtle);
      padding: var(--p-spacing-05) 0;
      margin: var(--p-spacing-05) 0 var(--p-spacing-07);
    }
    .counts div {
      margin: 0;
    }
    .counts dt {
      font-family: var(--s-font-mono);
      font-size: 0.6875rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--s-text-helper);
    }
    .counts dd {
      margin: var(--p-spacing-02) 0 0;
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      font-weight: 400;
    }
    .list {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--s-border-subtle);
    }
    .list li {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--s-border-subtle);
      padding: var(--p-spacing-05) 0;
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--p-spacing-05);
    }
    .tag {
      margin-left: auto;
      font-family: var(--s-font-mono);
      font-size: 0.625rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--s-text-helper);
      border: 1px solid var(--s-border-subtle);
      padding: 0 var(--p-spacing-02);
    }
  </style>
</Base>
